"""Blind seeing dialogues, round 4 (2026-10-23, written without the code, from docs/14 §3 "What Lumi sees",
the follow-up rows and §4, and knowledge/): every crowd evenly (adult, child, elderly, non_native, konglish, tester,
among_themselves = visitors who also talk to each other near Lumi; their remarks to each other are no-action turns).

Format: DIALOGUES = [{"who", "topic", "lang", "turns"}]; turn {"say", "scene", "route" (seeing / llm / act),
"expect_action", "must", "must_not", "check", "mix"}. scene: {"people": [{"id", "dist_m", "side", "top", "bottom",
"left_hand", "right_hand", "hands_visible", "raised"}], "objects": [{"name", "colour", "side", "dist_m"}]}; side as
Lumi sees it, hands are the person's own; "A" is the speaker. Scenes change between turns (people come and go, hands
change, things are moved or taken away, a jacket comes off): every answer from a fresh look. expect_action "none" or
a head command without "action:" ("look me | look center"). mix on every turn: plain (~60 %: clothes, hands, people,
things, distance, side, head commands), hard (~25 %: things that are not there, another colour, stale facts after
the scene changed, wrong claims to correct, "what's behind you", remarks and greetings that are no seeing question,
what a camera can't know: fingers, pockets; visitors talking to each other), slip (~15 %: whisper slips "genes",
typos, self-corrections "my shirt, no, my pants", "look left, no, right"). Distances allow +-0.3 m. Checked by
tests/dialogue_check.py turn loop with a fake scene per turn.

held: only scored, never read by whoever fixes the code.
"""

